{"type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Pittsburgh and Connellsville Railroad", "line": "Pittsburgh and Connellsville: Cumberland \u2013 Pittsburgh", "id": "pc-cumberland-pittsburgh", "color": "#00447C", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 35, "speed_source": "estimated: 1860s-era mountain-grade steam service; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1871, "end": 1872, "headway_min": 480, "note": "The Pittsburgh and Connellsville Railroad built along the Youghiogheny River between its namesake cities by 1860; the connecting Pennsylvania and Connellsville Railroad completed the missing link from Cumberland through to Pittsburgh in 1871, finally giving the B&O its own through route to Pittsburgh (part of company president John W. Garrett's post-Civil War expansion plans). Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baltimore_and_Ohio_Railroad"]}]}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-78.762383, 39.6526498], [-79.3567016, 39.8128548], [-79.6023538722341, 40.026764431377096], [-79.59665487761755, 40.03547323488812], [-79.59808194485527, 40.04025715244574], [-79.61154022312216, 40.04797807815837], [-79.62364039135511, 40.04678716496239], [-79.63128541965636, 40.03915435495269], [-79.63711448471328, 40.03737342235509], [-79.6660840740064, 40.050655311214484], [-79.67586425048083, 40.05287631595108], [-79.6833184735662, 40.06107718338067], [-79.68829355943481, 40.06169519555856], [-79.69477853628919, 40.052776415126324], [-79.69889060256884, 40.053032431625184], [-79.70233877096065, 40.06124127452387], [-79.71113594737292, 40.06395325984141], [-79.7253343136225, 40.07356311981746], [-79.7132882175628, 40.08024191941897], [-79.